{"codec":"JSON-syntax-dictionary-v4","atoms":["\"schema\"","\"issuer\"","\"isin\"","\"symbol\"","\"exchange_segment\"","\"research_cutoff\"","\"market_cutoff\"","\"price\"","\"shares\"","\"framework_sha256\"","\"ranking_eligible\"","\"classification\"","\"action\"","\"factors\"","\"gates\"","\"scores\"","\"financial_summary\"","\"model_summary\"","\"market_summary\"","\"source_ids\"","\"small-micro-cap-v3-source-safe-1\"","\"Rappid Valves (India) Limited\"","\"INE0MVO01012\"","\"RAPPID\"","\"NSE SME / SM\"","\"2026-10-20\"","\"2026-10-19\"","\"361\"","5191984","\"68d4de4255427df276318d0231530b867a453e740c74150e9768bf1387224137\"","false","\"Hold — unresolved\"","\"Research/watchlist only; not eligible for investment consideration on present evidence.\"","\"GOV\"","\"MOAT\"","\"REV\"","\"DUR\"","\"CAP\"","\"CASH\"","\"BAL\"","\"EXEC\"","\"EARN\"","\"R\"","\"D\"","\"P\"","\"L\"","\"score\"","\"confidence\"","\"material_facts\"","\"contrary\"","\"sources\"","4","\"Medium\"","\"Main opinions are unmodified, but India backup exceptions recur in FY24–26 and material filing/note errors persist.\"","\"IPO acquisition/capex money was redirected to working capital; old statutory dues and the Vinpra relationship warrant scrutiny.\"","\"No auditor-identified fraud or bank default; object variation received shareholder approval. September 2026 filing reports no pledge, NDU or other encumbrance, a dated positive not a blanket assurance.\"","\"S24\"","\"S25\"","\"S26\"","\"SOBJECT\"","\"SIPO\"","\"SSHP26\"","5","\"Customer qualification, marine engineering and product-specific factory approvals create useful switching friction.\"","\"Competitors have comparable industrial products and certifications; metal-price inflation was not fully passed through.\"","\"FY24 top-five customers represented 71.88% of sales. Purchase orders do not establish permanent contracts or market share.\"","\"SCALL\"","\"SUS\"","\"SHAWA\"","\"SKBL\"","8","\"FY21–26 nominal constant-entity operating sales grew from 7.6830956 to 53.233 crore, with no completed acquisition identified.\"","\"Manufacturing gross value added rose from 9.88681 to 14.06742 to 15.492 crore in FY24–26.\"","\"The pandemic depressed FY21. FY26 growth was 2.13%, with opposing half-year trends. This is nominal constant-scope growth, not verified volume growth: starting score 9, medium-confidence ceiling 8, no trajectory adjustment.\"","\"S22\"","\"SDECK\"","6","\"September firm backlog was 54.36 crore; BHEL orders span five ships through FY28.\"","\"Machining/testing purchases and US product qualification can broaden access.\"","\"Annual backlog rollforwards, order margins, advances and cancellations are not disclosed. US final approval remains pending.\"","\"SSEP\"","\"SBHEL\"","\"SJUL\"","\"Medium-low\"","\"Operating capital increased much faster than recent NOPAT; the one-year incremental return proxy fell to about 2.10%.\"","\"The calculation includes machinery and working capital, plus a separately disclosed lagged FY24–25 deployment proxy.\"","\"Project-level commissioning cohorts are not disclosed. The lagged proxy is stronger than the latest increment; score 4 reflects mixed observed returns, not proven destruction of every project.\"","1","\"High\"","\"FY24–26 cumulative CFO was negative 26.12514 crore against PAT of 16.64127 crore.\"","\"FY26 inventory rose 10.50486 crore and receivables 5.59962 crore despite only 1.1084 crore of sales growth.\"","\"Profits and orders are positive, and future collections could recover; neither reverses the observed cash conversion.\"","3","\"Debt was 17.843 crore against 0.387 crore cash/current-account proxy; deposit availability is unresolved.\"","\"Gross-payment timing and principal runoff expose funding gaps; the modeled equity rescue is optional and uncommitted.\"","\"Operating interest cover and book equity provide some protection. No actual current default has been established.\"","\"SMKT\"","\"MODEL\"","\"The February 2025 volume-growth target and June 2025 capex timetable were not demonstrated by FY26 results.\"","\"The June 2026 equipment timetable remained procurement/advance language in July; the IPO acquisition was not executed.\"","\"Export sales and formal marine orders grew. Management acknowledged the metal-price shock and missed growth.\"","\"SPROMISE\"","\"PAT grew from 6.03686 to 6.478 crore; year-end-share EPS rose from about 11.63 to 12.48 without FY26 issuance.\"","\"A useful-life estimate change, the FY25 weighted-share presentation and comparative errors limit earnings precision.\"","\"Operating profit supplies most earnings. Removing other income and adding a separate D&A stress still leaves positive profits; cash conversion is not double-penalized here.\"","null","\"Low\"","\"The primary base gross-cash path breaches before entry, so an ordinary investment IRR is not valid.\"","\"Optional post-entry equity cannot repair a past breach or become committed finance.\"","\"Some conditional deposit-access/slow-growth paths can be valued, but they do not establish a supported current base return.\"","2","\"Linked margin, collection, inventory and debt-maturity stress overwhelms cash and the bounded rescue.\"","\"Receivables and inventory are not a liquid equity floor against overdraft funding.\"","\"Product assets, profits and firm orders may retain value. There is no finding of actual insolvency or default.\"","\"Every candidate in the bounded cash-linked reverse search is retained, including failed paths.\"","\"No target is bracketed between adjacent cash-feasible samples in the stated 0–60% growth grids.\"","\"This is not proof that every nonmonotonic root is absent. Improved economics still rely on unverified existing-deposit availability; P remains NS.\"","\"The lower 60-session mean/median is median turnover 1,955,640 rupees; the five-lakh reference requires 5.1134 sessions at 5% participation, starting band 5.\"","\"A 600-share lot costs 216,600 rupees, more than twice the 97,782-rupee median daily participation allowance: one-point implementation deduction.\"","\"59 of 60 sessions traded. Spread and current surveillance clearance are unresolved; 2% and 10% participation sensitivities are provided.\"","\"G1\"","\"G2\"","\"G3\"","\"G4\"","\"status\"","\"reason\"","\"Conditional\"","\"Reporting/stewardship weaknesses are evidenced, but not abuse sufficient to establish Fail.\"","\"Material note, vintage and current cash-availability questions remain unresolved.\"","\"Scenario failure does not prove actual insolvency; the current cash/deposit/bank bridge is not verified.\"","\"Trade and lot data are verified; lot indivisibility, spread and current restriction gaps limit implementation assurance.\"","\"composites\"","\"judgment_sensitivities\"","\"rounding\"","\"BQS\"","\"GQS\"","\"IAS\"","\"weights\"","\"terms\"","\"raw\"","\"coverage\"","\"known_weighted_sum\"","\"lower_bound\"","\"upper_bound\"","\"cap\"","\"final\"","\"display\"","\"effective_lower_bound\"","\"effective_upper_bound\"","\"0.20\"","\"0.12\"","\"0.10\"","\"0.08\"","\"0.80\"","\"1.00\"","\"0.96\"","\"0.60\"","\"0.48\"","\"0.24\"","\"0.32\"","\"4.50\"","\"4.5\"","\"0.40\"","\"0.15\"","\"3.20\"","\"1.20\"","\"0.75\"","\"5.85\"","\"5\"","\"5.0\"","\"0.25\"","\"0.35\"","\"1.1250\"","\"0.55\"","\"1.9250\"","\"2.3750\"","\"6.4250\"","\"NS\"","\"factor\"","\"change\"","\"hypothetical_only\"","-1","true","\"raw_lower_bound\"","\"raw_upper_bound\"","\"4.30\"","\"3\"","\"2.00\"","\"6.05\"","\"4.70\"","\"2.4250\"","\"6.4750\"","\"4.38\"","\"5.70\"","\"2.3450\"","\"6.3950\"","\"4.62\"","\"6.00\"","\"2.4050\"","\"6.4550\"","\"Display one decimal; use exact unrounded values for every downstream calculation.\"","\"units\"","\"revenue_cagr_5y\"","\"revenue_cagr_3y\"","\"incremental_roic_3y\"","\"lagged_FY24_FY25_deployment_proxy\"","\"lagged_proxy_caveat\"","\"five_year_incremental_roic\"","\"three_year_cfo\"","\"three_year_pat\"","\"three_year_capex\"","\"current_market_cap\"","\"fy26_normalized_pat_D