"","3556016","\"RevisedQ1FY27 business update\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_10072026150526_GBU_Rappid_Signed.pdf\"","\"2026-07-10\"","\"All six pages: correction from revenue to sales; firm backlog 40 crore versus customer confirmations of 11 crore pending purchase orders.\"","\"a5c092f33b3b6cfdee6fca21a1f3e553e461dc7532377bcb9b223d2dccfa7bcc\"","1173565","\"September21 orderandbacklog filing\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_21092026153828_Work_Order.pdf\"","\"All three pages and order annexures; firm backlog 54.36 crore.\"","\"ab1d75fc9374c9ded92d1b184a0f36476366eb8c7f52069a098441a5fc5d317f\"","380861","\"L&T order filing\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_13082026191053_Workorder.pdf\"","\"Both pages: ten-week delivery starts after drawing and QAP approval.\"","\"9039cf5e21f4722e7c8504fff4d17f9b8cabd9bfc2682277fa30a8d0a4228521\"","695508","\"BHEL FleetSupportShip order\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_15062026102327_Work_Order.pdf\"","\"2026-06-15\"","\"Dated June 13, exchange filing June 15: 18.0576 crore, three shipsets around one year and two in FY27–28.\"","\"f9c6ea3e04903b4660808ccdeb672cb00b40b4c8400c851aa6bc4b3aafdc88cb\"","353664","\"Shree order formalization\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_08062026151443_Work_Order_Shree_.pdf\"","\"2026-06-08\"","\"Formal 8.55 crore order, approximately one-year delivery; supersedes LOI status in June 1 call.\"","\"85b6d67f3a5e378d9f221793a38f1f6aa5c1d2a1734fda23b7e8b22e781327f8\"","690756","\"FY26 annual encumbrance declaration\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/team_sandeshc_29042026124914_40.pdf\"","\"2026-05-25\"","\"April 6 declaration says no encumbrance created during FY26. It is not a September 30 zero-balance statement.\"","\"87ceecce21f8dbea04ffaddb5377407fceb53b8cc3ae3df2f7c37fa28b4cb62b\"","941249","\"January2026 financial filing clarification\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_19012026164650_Clarification_Letter_Signed.pdf\"","\"2026-01-19\"","\"Single business segment; reporting omission acknowledged. Subject says quarter but the clarification concerns the September half-year.\"","\"6862f2847bebc10788b4efcc4ee3f61bd40adc2bcaa3bdccbbc4388cb0b28df1\"","234491","\"June2025 financial filing clarification\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_25062025164758_Claritifcationletterrappidsd.pdf\"","\"2025-06-25\"","\"June 25 signed response admits omitted unmodified-opinion declaration; disputes or seeks guidance on half-year/balancing-figure format queries.\"","\"1dd69612b24fe16b757786608b79465a07dcb3848d3eb121eb760fd1c5959c94\"","1446038","\"February2025 business guidance\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RAPPID_01022025120242_RappidQIA.pdf\"","\"2025-02-01\"","\"February 2025 guidance: 50% volume CAGR target for FY26/FY27, foundry talks, and June 2025 capex completion expectation.\"","\"5a8ef64b5caccf3865b8ebbc85aae86730a6891b4d64218bfcfc5bb7b3b6dbcc\"","607529","\"IPO objects variation vote\"","\"https://www.rappidvalves.in/assets/img/uploads/announcement/16d56-change-in-ipo-object_scrutinizer-result.pdf\"","\"All pages: March 31–April 29 postal ballot, April 30 result; inconsistent with annual-report April 17 EGM description.\"","\"2a08e5a28cc9e01b4fa8b614c69d101a7841a2cbb07ec7dbaedd73d86e08ef87\"","782323","\"US qualification status\"","\"https://www.rappidvalves.in/assets/img/uploads/announcement/cc2e2-strategic-business-update_rappid_sd.pdf\"","\"All four pages: final sampling/testing for product/factory approval; commercial orders not yet assured.\"","\"10fdb77a1a81f9c0d70c9f1200e465f25c8259b24f22d501cd534bf35f86e73f\"","404562","\"NSE shareholding-pattern table\"","\"https://www.nseindia.com/companies-listing/corporate-filings-shareholding-pattern\"","\"NSE SME table filtered for RAPPID: September 30 promoter 51.73%, public 48.27%, filed October 12. Earlier failed XML retrieval is superseded by SSHP26.\"","\"NSE linked September2026 XBRL\"","\"primary; duplicate locator of SSHP26\"","\"Same primary September XBRL as SSHP26; aggregate contents subsequently verified. No personal shareholder rows retained.\"","\"NSE October19 security master\"","\"Issuer-only ISIN row. All 60 daily source URLs, complete archive hashes and issuer fields are in market_extract.json.\"","\"KirloskarBrothersFY26 integrated report\"","\"https://www.kirloskarpumps.com/virtual-annual-report-2026/\"","\"FY2026\"","\"Manufacturing, R&D, distribution and valve-product breadth; qualitative economic benchmark only.\"","\"HawaEngineersFY25annualreport\"","\"https://hawaengltd.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/FINAL_Hawa_Engineers_Ltd___AR___2024-25.pdf\"","\"2025-09\"","\"Page 28: FY25 revenue 121.0618 crore, EBITDA including other income 6.2397, finance 2.9774, PAT 1.5958. Historical FY25, not current FY26.\"","\"NSE September 2026 shareholding XBRL, aggregate facts only\"","\"Quarter ended 30 September 2026; aggregate promoter, encumbrance and lock-in fields\"","\"Atam Valves FY2026 audited standalone results\"","\"https://www.atamvalves.in/wp-content/uploads/Atam_Valves_Limited_FinancialResults_31032026.pdf\"","\"Physical pages 3–5 P&L, balance sheet and cash flow; limited economic comparison, not full peer audit\"","\"reading_method\"","\"annual_audits\"","\"forensic_reconciliations\"","\"rpt_history_crore\"","\"unknowns\"","\"Signed main opinions, statutory reporting paragraphs and all supplied CARO/IFC annexures were read, not merely directors summaries. Original scanned audit pages were visually checked where OCR was unclear. The exchange FY26 copy independently corroborates the issuer copy.\"","\"main\"","\"caro\"","\"ifc\"","\"effect\"","\"auditor\"","\"2019\"","\"FY19 signed opinion unavailable in this bundle. The appended main report explicitly concerns FY18.\"","\"FY18 Annexure A is referenced; no FY19 assurance can be inferred.\"","\"Appended positive IFC opinion concerns FY18 only.\"","\"Retain the FY19 audit-vintage gap; do not describe eight consecutive clean annual audits.\"","\"Amrut Deshmukh, 5 September 2018 (appended FY18 report)\"","\"2020\"","\"Parab & Kadam / Prasad Parab, 5 October 2020\"","\"Unmodified main opinion.\"","\"Inventory verification procedures reasonable but not adequate. PF, ESIC and professional-tax arrears beyond six months cover 2016–20. No bank default reported.\"","\"No separately verified positive IFC conclusion; do not infer it from the main opinion.\"","\"Directors report names Kalantri, unlike the signed audit. Historic arrears and inventory-control weakness matter; no allegation of invented inventory.\"","\"2021\"","\"Kalantri Assawa & Associates, 30 October 2021\"","\"Main report calls CARO inapplicable, yet an annexure records irregular PF/ESIC/professional-tax deposits and dues beyond six months through FY21. Remuneration paragraph is incomplete boilerplate. No fraud or bank default reported.\"","\"No separately verified positive IFC opinion.\"","\"Boilerplate inconsistency and old dues are not erased by later unmodified opinions.\"","\"2022\"","\"Vijay Bhardwaj & Co, 26 September 2022\"","\"Stated inapplicable; no separate annexure supplied.\"","\"No separate positive IFC opinion supplied.\"","\"The private-company report does not establish when earlier arrears were paid.\"","\"2023\"","\"Vijay Bhardwaj & Co, 6 September 2023\"","\"Stated inapplicable.\"","\"The adequacy paragraph is grammatically incomplete, not positive assurance.\"","\"Original accounts differ from subsequent comparatives and IPO restatement. All vintages are preserved.\"","\"2024\"","\"KAVA & Associates, 12 June 2024\"","\"Unmodified main opinion; other legal/books reporting explicitly notes missing daily backup in India.\"","\"TDS 1,437,671 rupees and PF 19,454 rupees overdue more than six months. No bank default or fraud reported.\"","\"Exemption asserted, not a separate positive assurance opinion.\"","\"Recurring backup and statutory-dues concerns; cash-flow/debt classifications require reconciliation.\"","\"2025\"","\"KAVA & Associates, 12 May 2025\"","\"Unmodified main opinion; daily electronic backup in India exception repeats.\"","\"No internal-audit system asserted despite corporate/board references. No fraud or bank default reported.\"","\"Appended adequacy opinion is distinct from compliance with every legal/books requirement.\"","\"Private-company remuneration-exemption wording persists despite conversion/listing. June 25 clarification admits missing opinion declaration but disputes or requests guidance on other exchange format queries.\"","\"2026\"","\"S26,SN26\"","\"KAVA & Associates / Vivek Jalan, 27 May 2026\"","\"Unmodified main opinion; required daily India-located electronic backup was not maintained. Positive audit-trail operation/non-tampering is a separate test.\"","\"No inventory discrepancy of at least 10%; quarterly working-capital returns generally agree. Some statutory delays, but no dues older than six months reported. No bank default, wilful-default finding, fraud, ADT-4 report or auditor resignation. No identified one-year material uncertainty, expressly not a guarantee. No internal-audit system conflicts with named internal auditor.\"","\"Separate adequate and effective IFC opinion.\"","\"Do not call this blanket clean-books assurance. Note errors and capital-allocation changes remain material; later dues language does not prove old payment dates.\"","\"issue\"","\"evidence\"","\"treatment\"","\"FY22–24 IPO restatement\"","\"SIPO F1–F13\"","\"Keep original and restated PAT, equity and CFO separate. Restated CFO is before finance; subtract finance only to create the comparable after-finance series. FY24: −1.0733 −1.4029 = −2.4762 versus later −2.48153, residual −0.00533 crore. Do not silently plug the difference.\"","\"FY26 and FY25 EPS\"","\"S26 P&L and Note 30; S25 Note 30\"","\"FY26 computed EPS is 6.478 crore /5,191,984 shares, about 12.48 rupees; the face P&L figure 0.1 is a scale error. FY25 uses the year-end share count despite a midyear IPO. A year-end-share comparator is not true weighted-average EPS.\"","\"Unbilled revenue\"","\"S26 Notes 18 and 21\"","\"Note 21 gross opening/closing 5,267.8/5,309.7 lakh conflict with Note 18 actual 119.4/161.3 lakh. The net 41.9 lakh agrees. Use Note 18 levels, not the erroneous gross note.\"","\"Depreciation estimate\"","\"S26 Note 2.6 and asset schedule; SDECK\"","\"A prospective useful-life/residual estimate change is disclosed; precise profit benefit is ND. An additional 0.15 crore pretax D&A sensitivity is analytical, not the asserted official benefit. Rounded H2 D&A is 0.12 crore versus H1 0.52.\"","\"IPO proceeds\"","\"S26 Note 32; SOBJECT\"","\"Remaining 7.6451 crore capex/acquisition authorization was varied to working capital. Voting closed April 29 and results were disclosed April 30; do not use the annual-report April 17 EGM date as earlier approval. Existing deposits of 6.876 crore may overlap IPO/collateral restrictions. Authorization is not new cash.\"","\"Share chronology\"","\"S25 capital history; SIPO; S26 Note 3; SMKT\"","\"The 2024 preference transaction of 4.98 crore involved 302,184 new ordinary shares at 164.80 rupees, followed by the September 2024 IPO of 1,369,800 shares at 222. FY26 narrative misdates 2025 and mixes preference units into opening ordinary counts. Verified current ordinary shares are 5,191,984.\"","\"Debt service coverage\"","\"S26 Note 36\"","\"Printed principal/numerator data have unit/formula inconsistencies. Do not use that DSCR as assurance. The model explicitly dates principal cash outflows.\"","\"Guarantees\"","\"S26 Notes 34 and 37\"","\"The explicit 0.146 crore performance bank guarantee overrides generic no-contingencies wording. It is not automatically debt; a call is a distinct stress.\"","\"Related-party customer\"","\"SIPO Annexure XXIX, F29\"","\"Vinpra sales were 7.657 crore in FY24, 0.0835 in FY23 and 0.0019 in FY22. FY24 closing trade receivable was 1.5893 crore, from opening 0.0208, debits 8.9474 and credits 7.3789. Credits are not automatically bank receipts. A September 2022 directorship resignation does not itself resolve influence. Latest relationship/customer status is ND; no unsupported round-tripping allegation.\"","\"Gaurav_professional\"","\"Mansi_professional\"","\"Mansi_salary\"","\"Vijay_professional\"","\".195\"","\".190\"","\".005\"","\".033\"","\".225\"","\".1375\"","\".135\"","\"Gaurav_salary\"","\"Vijay_salary\"","\".1263\"","\".0855\"","\".0485\"","\"Mansi_rent\"","\"independent_directors_total\"","\".48\"","\".0286\"","\".06\"","\"Mansi_remuneration\"","\".62\"","\".28\"","\".026\"","\".054\"","\"Complete signed FY19 audit\"","\"Full reconciliation of original FY23 and later comparative figures\"","\"Current deposit lien, use restrictions, maturities and bank confirmations\"","\"Overdraft sanction, renewal, covenants and undrawn committed capacity\"","\"Inventory aging and obsolescence\"","\"Latest customer concentration and Vinpra relationship/collection status\"","\"Quantified useful-life estimate profit benefit\"","\"Tax-litigation closure documents\"","\"caps\"","\"composite\"","\"ceiling\"","\"trigger\"","\"preserve_NS\"","\"CASH = 1: persistent negative three-year cash conversion despite reported profits.\"","\"operating_ebit\"","\"operating_ebitda\"","\"ebitda_margin\"","\"normalized_pat\"","\"nopat\"","\"cfo_comparable\"","\"owner_cash_after_all_capex\"","\"year_end_current_share_eps_comparator\"","\"interest_cover\"","\"0.0240161\"","\"0.2706548\"","\"0.2145507\"","\"0.1344301\"","\"-0.4598619\"","\"0.5111943\"","\"1.3370404\"","\"1.4714705\"","\"0.191520524617707477178860041777952106\"","\"0.184979025\"","\"1.002780300\"","\"0.413234516901438833401643764695730958\"","\"1.22619067816933887758979099170516700\"","\"revenue_addition\"","\"revenue_growth\"","\"roce_average_debt_plus_equity\"","\"roe_average_equity\"","\"0.0113\"","\"0.2899\"","\"0.28